WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.628 --> 00:00:04.379
Lisey's Story is my favorite.

00:00:05.172 --> 00:00:06.673
It always has been.

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:09.051
At its core, this is a love story.

00:00:10.344 --> 00:00:12.429
It's a story of a woman's courage,

00:00:13.138 --> 00:00:17.684
who would do almost anything
to save her husband's life and sanity.

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:27.027
Lisey is a different thing for me.

00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:29.488
It's very close to my heart.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:33.200
I had pneumonia around the year 2000

00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:36.203
and came really close to stepping out.

00:00:36.912 --> 00:00:38.997
When I came home from the hospital,

00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:41.416
my wife had cleaned out my study.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.751
and I thought to myself,

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:45.295
"I've died. I'm a ghost."

00:00:48.549 --> 00:00:50.968
And the idea for Lisey's Story
came from that,

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:55.430
particularly the idea that writers,
when they make things up,

00:00:55.639 --> 00:00:57.140
they go to a different world.

00:01:03.689 --> 00:01:05.691
I wanted to tell the story
that was in the book,

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:07.067
but I wanted to make it better.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.778
I thought if somebody was
going to mess it up,

00:01:09.862 --> 00:01:13.448
I used to tell my wife,
"Nobody's going to mess it up but me."

00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:22.916
The story of Scott's childhood,
when he finally tells it,

00:01:23.041 --> 00:01:24.710
is particularly horrific.

00:01:27.004 --> 00:01:29.756
He retreats into this fantasy world.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.801
Boo'ya Moon is his secret place.

00:01:32.885 --> 00:01:35.095
It's a place that's very,
very beautiful,

00:01:35.721 --> 00:01:38.182
and at the same time,
very dangerous.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.398
It's a very scary story,

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:47.524
in a lot of ways.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.485
It's scary in a supernatural way,

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:52.362
but it's also scary because...

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:55.574
there really are
dangerous people out there.

00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:01.872
Lisey's Story could only have come
from the mind of Stephen King.

00:02:02.331 --> 00:02:04.041
It's beautiful and haunting,

00:02:04.208 --> 00:02:05.959
and romantic and horrifying.

00:02:06.877 --> 00:02:09.755
When I think of Lisey's Story,
like I think of Stephen King,

00:02:10.172 --> 00:02:12.216
and how is this connected with his life.

00:02:12.841 --> 00:02:14.051
It was a lot of pressure, too.

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:16.762
We wanted to make sure
that we did him justice,

00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:18.305
and that we did the story justice.

00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:19.681
I'm a visual writer.

00:02:19.765 --> 00:02:22.684
I'm interested in
the power of the imagination.

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:26.188
We can talk about it as
otherworldly and fantastic.

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:28.941
He's like,
"Oh, no, it's real. It's real."

